{"indicator":"pedestrians","unit":"%","years":[2021],"latestWithin":5,"notes":{"TWN":"台灣用交通部的 30 日內死亡人數（每年都有）：行人死亡 2022 年 394 人、2025 年 354 人（占 12.4%）。2022 年 12 月 CNN 的旅遊專欄引用網友的說法，形容台灣是「行人地獄」（a living hell for pedestrians），這個說法之後在國內廣泛流傳，也帶動民間對行人安全的訴求。交通部 2023 年 8 月向行政院提出「行人交通安全政策綱領」（2024–2027 年），《道路交通安全基本法》2023 年 12 月公布、2024 年 1 月 1 日施行，以 2050 年道路交通事故零死亡為目標。"},"notesEn":{"TWN":"Taiwan uses Ministry of Transportation and Communications deaths within 30 days (every year): 394 pedestrians died in 2022 and 354 in 2025 (12.4% of road deaths). In December 2022 a CNN travel column quoted a description of Taiwan as \"a living hell for pedestrians\"; the phrase spread widely in Taiwan and fed public calls for safer streets. The Ministry presented a pedestrian traffic safety policy framework (2024–2027) to the Executive Yuan in August 2023, and the Road Traffic Safety Basic Act, promulgated in December 2023 and in force from 1 January 2024, sets a goal of zero road deaths by 2050."},"encoding":"delta","values":{"ALB":[-1,193],"DZA":[0,25],"ATG":[0,43],"ARG":[-1,109],"ARM":[-1,318],"AUS":[0,12],"AUT":[-1,102],"AZE":[0,42],"BHS":[0,28],"BHR":[-1,226],"BGD":[-1,322],"BRB":[-1,222],"BLR":[-1,413],"BEL":[-1,145],"BLZ":[-1,248],"BEN":[0,18],"BTN":[-1,34],"BOL":[-1,25],"BIH":[-1,273],"BWA":[-1,247],"BRA":[-1,146],"VGB":[0,0],"BGR":[-1,168],"KHM":[0,null],"CAN":[-1,162],"CAF":[0,0],"CHL":[0,23],"CHN":[-1,289],"COL":[-1,215],"COM":[-1,261],"COK":[0,0],"CRI":[-1,247],"CIV":[-1,402],"HRV":[-1,127],"CUB":[-1,304],"CYP":[-1,221],"CZE":[-1,213],"COD":[-1,519],"DNK":[-1,146],"DMA":[0,17],"DOM":[0,12],"ECU":[0,9],"EGY":[0,25],"SLV":[-1,346],"ERI":[0,25],"EST":[0,24],"SWZ":[-1,438],"ETH":[-1,367],"FIN":[0,11],"FRA":[-1,141],"GEO":[-1,265],"DEU":[-1,134],"GHA":[0,null],"GRC":[0,null],"GTM":[0,30],"GUY":[-1,283],"HND":[-1,337],"HUN":[0,25],"ISL":[-1,222],"IND":[-1,189],"IDN":[0,0],"IRN":[-1,198],"IRQ":[0,28],"IRL":[-1,186],"ISR":[-1,269],"ITA":[-1,164],"JAM":[-1,197],"JPN":[-1,354],"JOR":[-1,287